course: dictionary
lesson: 13509
title: The word immobility
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Immobility means not moving, or not being able to move. The clue is in the start of the word: im- means not, and mobility is about moving. «The injured bird lay in total immobility under the hedge.» The bird could not move, so immobility means being stuck still.
explain: Immobility can also be a choice. «The hunter waited in complete immobility, so the deer did not notice him.» The hunter kept still on purpose. Ask yourself: is the person unable to move, or are they choosing to keep still? The sentence usually tells you which.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The injured bird lay in stillness under the hedge» makes sense, so immobility means stillness. «Her long immobility showed she was too frightened to run» shows that stillness can also show fear.
fact: Immobility is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say «total immobility», not «an immobility».
fact: «Immobility» means the state of not moving or not being able to move.
fact: «Immobility» can also mean keeping very still on purpose, like a hidden animal or a careful hunter.
fact: In health lessons, long periods of immobility can be dangerous, because a body that stays still for too long can become weak or stiff.
fact: The prefix im- means not, so immobile means not moving, and immobility is the noun for that state.
exercise: «The injured bird lay in total immobility under the hedge.» What does immobility mean here? | Eating quickly | *Not being able to move | Flying high in the sky | Singing loudly
exercise: «The hunter waited in complete immobility, so the deer did not notice him.» Why did the hunter keep so still? | He was dancing | *He wanted to stay hidden | He had lost his shoes | He was too tired to walk
exercise: The word immobility starts with im-. What does im- mean? | Again | *Not | Very | Under
test: «Her long immobility showed she was too frightened to run.» What feeling does the immobility show? | Boredom | Joy | *Fear | Anger
test: After a bad fall, a boy cannot move at all. Which phrase describes his state? | *Total immobility | Total laughter | Loud shouting | Quick running
exam: «After the crash, the driver's immobility worried the doctors, who feared his legs were badly hurt.» What does immobility mean in this sentence? | Driving very fast | Talking loudly to the doctors | *Being unable to move | Feeling no pain at all
